messages:
emily_sales: Ivan from Helix reported the POC stream failing during their mobile demo. Webview throws JSON.parse errors and the stream cuts out after ~40s.
tom_se: Can you paste client logs and a network capture? Is desktop affected or just the embedded webview?
ivan_customer: Only our Android webview so far. Error: "SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at parseEvent (bundle.js:128)". Network shows SSE events but some data lines end mid-object. Sample copied below.
ivan_customer: event: message
data: {"idx":5,"text":"Hello world"}

event: message
data: {"idx":6,"text":"This is a very lon

"

client then fails trying to JSON.parse the second payload.
rachel_oncall: Infra side: I see a brief spike of 429s and a few connection resets on the edge proxy at the same time. LB logs show "upstream timed out" and "connection reset by peer". Could be proxy buffering + client retries.
tom_se: Two likely contributors: (1) client assumes each data: payload is a full JSON object and parses immediately, (2) proxy or network fragmentation is splitting payloads. Short-term fixes: change the webview handler to buffer data lines and attempt JSON.parse only when buffer forms valid JSON, and ask the customer's proxy to disable response buffering and increase keepalive.
infra-bot: deploy v2.18.0 canary eu-west-1 at 2106309800
rachel_oncall: On our side I'll temporarily reduce retry concurrency for that org and enable periodic SSE heartbeats (comment lines) to keep connections alive. I'll also add a quick metric to track partial-parse errors.
tom_se: I'll send a tiny accumulator snippet for the webview they can drop in without rebuilding: ```js
let buf = '';
function onSseData(line) {
  buf += line;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(buf);
    handle(obj);
    buf = '';
  } catch(e) {
    // still partial
    if (buf.length > 64*1024) { buf = ''; }
  }
}
```
emily_sales: Ivan, want us to apply the infra tweak and share the snippet? We can also do a short maintenance window if needed.
ivan_customer: Please apply infra changes and send snippet. We'll try the shim and report back in 30m. Thanks!
